@@ -0,0 +1,7 @@
+# Spec: JSON Patch conformance review
+**Standard**: RFC 6902 §3, §4.1–4.6, §5; RFC 6901.
+Review of `applyPatch` found and fixed:
+- Sparse-array holes in a patch were silently skipped; now rejected (each element must be an operation object, §3/§4).
+- `op`/`path`/`from`/`value` were read through the prototype chain; only own members count now.
+- `replace` was remove+add, which moved the member to the end of the object; now replaced in place (§4.3).
+Tests: `test/patch.test.js` ("conformance"). No public API change.
